  "safety_invariants": [
    "script/model layers cannot call buy/sell order-intent primitives",
    "script layer rejects entry/exit execution primitives",
    "automation buy/sell creates only an order-intent object",
    "risk evaluation is mandatory before policy and execution",
    "PAPER and ARMED cannot submit broker execution",
    "LIVE requires explicit lifecycle activation plus host live-execution guard",
    "system actor cannot activate LIVE",
    "execution intent is an authority record, not a broker request",
    "IDE automation preview is paper-only and never submits broker execution",
    "signals carry explainability provenance without altering runtime semantics",
    "CoreSpirit owns neutral market-data contracts and does not import broker domain types",
    "historical/replay/realtime hosts execute the same validated artifact through the same VM",
    "signals are normalized into immutable sequenced deduplicable envelopes",
    "broker connectivity is available only through a host-owned execution adapter"
